# Knowledge Base: Connected / Disconnected Satellite — CA Bundle & Hammer ISS Sync

This KB covers three operational topics for an **Inter-Satellite Sync (ISS) network sync** layout:

1. Trusting **self-signed** Satellite HTTPS certificates for remote `hammer`
2. **Listing** repositories added on the disconnected Satellite
3. **Synchronizing** those repositories (ISS pull from connected → disconnected)

All `hammer` examples below are intended to be **run on the connected Satellite**, while **targeting the disconnected Satellite API** with `--server`.

Replace placeholders:

| Placeholder | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| `YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD` | Admin password on disconnected Satellite |
| `sampleorg` | Organization name (use your real org name) |
| FQDNs below | Match your DNS / install hostnames |

Example hostnames used in this document:

- **Connected Satellite:** `connected-satellite.example.com` (synced from Red Hat CDN; upstream for ISS)
- **Disconnected Satellite:** `disconnected-satellite.example.com` (CDN / content source pointed at connected; pulls via ISS network sync)

---

## Architecture (short)

```
Red Hat CDN ──sync──► Connected Satellite ──ISS network sync──► Disconnected Satellite
                         (has CDN access)                         (no direct CDN; uses connected)
```

| Role | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| **Connected Satellite** | Registers to Red Hat, enables products/repos, syncs content from the CDN. Acts as the **upstream content source** for disconnected. |
| **Disconnected Satellite** | Manifest imported locally. Content credentials / CDN URL configured to the **connected** Satellite. Enables the same (or subset) repos and **syncs from connected** over the network (ISS). |

**Important:** Enabling a repository on disconnected does **not** download packages by itself. You must run a **repository/product synchronize** on disconnected so it pulls content from connected. Connected must already have those repos synced from the CDN (or the pull will be empty / fail).

