## 2. Remote hammer pattern (CLI on connected → API on disconnected)

Define a reusable prefix (connected shell):

```bash
export HAMMER_DISC=(
  hammer
  --server https://disconnected-satellite.example.com
  --username admin
  --password 'YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD'
)

ORG=sampleorg
```

Examples below use `"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}"` and `"$ORG"`.

---

## 3. List all added repositories (on disconnected, via remote hammer)

“Added” repositories are those **enabled** under the organization (from the subscription manifest / repository sets).

### List repository instances (what will sync)
```bash
# Human-readable table
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository list --organization "$ORG"

# CSV (includes Id — useful for sync-by-id)
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv repository list --organization "$ORG"
```

### List enabled repository sets (what was turned on from the manifest)
```bash
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository-set list \
  --organization "$ORG" \
  --enabled true
```

### List products and how many repos each has
```bash
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product list --organization "$ORG"
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv product list --organization "$ORG"
```

### Optional: confirm org name/label
```bash
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" organization list
```

Use the **Title/Name** that matches your environment as `"$ORG"` (this KB uses `sampleorg` as a stand-in).

---

## 4. Sync all added repositories (ISS pull on disconnected)

Connected must already have the same content synced from the CDN. Disconnected sync jobs pull from the configured upstream (connected).

### Option A — Sync by product (recommended)

Sync every product that currently has one or more repositories:

```bash
ORG=sampleorg

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv product list --organization "$ORG" \
  | awk -F, 'NR>1 && $5+0 > 0 {print $2}' \
  | while IFS= read -r product; do
      echo "=== Syncing product: ${product} ==="
      "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
        --name "$product" \
        --organization "$ORG" \
        --async
    done
```

`$5` in the CSV is the **Repositories** count column from `hammer --csv product list`. Adjust the column index if your hammer CSV headers differ (`hammer --csv product list --organization "$ORG" | head -1`).

### Option B — Sync every repository by ID

```bash
ORG=sampleorg

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv repository list --organization "$ORG" \
  | awk -F, 'NR>1 {print $1}' \
  | while IFS= read -r id; do
      echo "=== Syncing repository id=${id} ==="
      "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository synchronize \
        --id "$id" \
        --organization "$ORG" \
        --async
    done
```

### Explicit product sync examples

```bash
ORG=sampleorg

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
  --name "Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64" \
  --organization "$ORG" \
  --async

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
  --name "Red Hat Satellite" \
  --organization "$ORG" \
  --async

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
  --name "Red Hat Satellite Capsule" \
  --organization "$ORG" \
  --async
```

### Monitor sync tasks on disconnected

```bash
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task list --search 'state = running' --organization "$ORG"

"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task list \
  --search 'label ~ Actions::Katello::Repository::Sync' \
  --organization "$ORG" | head

# Follow a specific task:
# "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task progress --id <TASK_UUID>
# "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task info --id <TASK_UUID>
```

### After sync — re-check repository state

```bash
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository list --organization "$ORG"
"${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product info \
  --name "Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64" \
  --organization "$ORG"
```

